  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "This survey reviews ~100+ quantum machine learning experiments executed on real hardware across domains such as high‑energy physics, healthcare, and finance. Reported implementations typically use 1–61 qubits on superconducting or ion‑trap devices with shallow circuits; example results include VQC event classification with ~3 qubits achieving AUC ≈ 0.80 and QSVM with 15 qubits achieving AUC ≈ 0.831 on small datasets. The paper concludes that current QML implementations show comparable performance to classical baselines but no demonstrated quantum advantage due to noise, limited qubit counts, and data‑loading overhead.",
